# Q9 — Does Session.Info report cost + token counts for the chosen model?
Date: 2026-10-13. Container agency-spike-q9 (agency-base:2.0.26, bridge,
same-path worktree mount). Model that runs: opencode/cat-jam-free.
AGENCY_MODEL proper: opencode-go/muse-spark-1.3-contributor (quota-blocked, see below).

## Commands + trimmed output

$ curl -X POST /api/session {"title":"q9","agent":"spike",
  "model":{"providerID":"opencode","id":"cat-jam-free"},"location":{...}}
{"data":{"id":"ses_ec8f67df9ffeyjBTuZVYS3dF43",...}}          # HTTP 200

$ curl /api/session/ses_ec8f67df9ffeyjBTuZVYS3dF43   # pre-run
{"data":{"id":"ses_ec8f67df9ffeyjBTuZVYS3dF43",...,
  "cost":0,
  "tokens":{"input":0,"output":0,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":0,"write":0}},...}}

$ curl -X POST /api/session/<id>/prompt {"text":"Reply with exactly: q9-marker"}
HTTP 200
$ curl -X POST /api/experimental/session/<id>/wait
HTTP 204   (assistant finish: stop, error: null; transcript holds q9-marker)

$ curl /api/session/ses_ec8f67df9ffeyjBTuZVYS3dF43   # post-run
{"data":{"id":"ses_ec8f67df9ffeyjBTuZVYS3dF43",...,
  "cost":0,
  "tokens":{"input":1814,"output":4,"reasoning":26,"cache":{"read":896,"write":0}},
  "outcome":"succeeded",...}}

$ # AGENCY_MODEL leg (same container, same prompt shape)
$ curl -X POST /api/session {"title":"q9-go","agent":"spike",
  "model":{"providerID":"opencode-go","id":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor"},...}
{"data":{"id":"ses_ec8f65cb6ffetZq4wYr275l5EN",...}}          # HTTP 200
$ curl .../prompt ... ; curl .../wait
HTTP 204
$ curl /api/session/ses_ec8f65cb6ffetZq4wYr275l5EN/message  (assistant, trimmed)
finish: error | {"type":"provider.quota","message":"Go usage limit exceeded",
  "status":429,...GoUsageLimitError...limitName: monthly...}
$ curl /api/session/ses_ec8f65cb6ffetZq4wYr275l5EN
{"data":{...,"cost":0,
  "tokens":{"input":0,"output":0,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":0,"write":0}},
  "outcome":"failed",...}}

## Observation
- The mechanism works: after a real run Session.Info reports cost plus
  filled-in token counts (input/output/reasoning/cache.read). The running
  model is a free tier, so cost stays 0 while tokens fill in.
- For AGENCY_MODEL itself the fill-in is untestable right now: the account's
  Go monthly usage limit is exhausted (429 GoUsageLimitError), the turn
  fails, and cost/tokens stay zeroed. Nothing about the reporting path looks
  model-specific (same Session.Info shape, same zeroed pre-run fields).

## Verdict: partly (reporting proven with the running model; AGENCY_MODEL
fill-in pending quota reset; tokens-only fallback not needed)
